  "checks": [
    "Ten source/global/minimum settings, Q3 and JA, ordinary/meta/patchmeta/maxarea, one/four workers. Check every emitted surface against expected spacing and require every fixture material.",
    "Shader sizes 16/32/48, entity bases/scales, global fallback, positive fractional truncation, minimum clamps, 1e38 scale, large entity base and minimum above the supported maximum.",
    "Subdivision, material clones/back sides, curved patches, transformed brush models, imported forced-meta meshes, same-shader adjacent func_groups, authored overrides and vertex-lit surfaces.",
    "Verify group source-space ownership and prohibit an emitted surface crossing regions with differing effective spacing. Equal clamped spacing may merge.",
    "New triangular projected decals receive initial classification after the -maxarea shortcut; an intermediate implementation failing this case was repaired before final validation.",
    "Final native reports agree exactly on effective values and selected atlas UV spans across all three configurations. Worker comparisons cover normalized native BSP lumps and complete SRF bytes."
  ],
