  "limits": [
    "Affected maps intentionally change inherited sampling and can repack lightmaps; no universal legacy byte-compatibility claim is made.",
    "SRF sampleSize describes requested effective sampling. LIGHT can still enlarge sampling for atlas constraints. Selected atlas checks use an unclamped 64-unit planar face at spacing 64.",
    "Ordinary-mode model validation stops at BSP/SRF because of the separately reproduced existing model issue. The twelve atlas checks use meta, patchmeta and maxarea.",
    "Existing generated-decal/model inheritance policy, source numeric parsing, minimum/maximum syntax and GUI preview resolution are not redesigned.",
    "Native control fixtures do not qualify arbitrary maps, lighting seam quality, engine pixels, fur/skybox rendering or Radiant inherited-density previews.",
    "Linux ASan/UBSan uses the established leak-detection exclusion. No game, OS screenshot or user-input control was used."
